Number Format
Number Format controls how a value is displayed in a cell.
Types of Number Formats
General (Default Format)
•	Default format in Excel
•	No specific formatting
•	Displays numbers as entered
Ex:
      100
Number
•	Used for normal numbers
•	Can set:
o	Decimal places
o	1000 separator (,)
Example:
1000 → 1,000
25 → 25.00
Currency
•	Adds currency symbol
•	Used for money values
Example:
1000 → ₹1,000.00
1000 → $1,000.00
Used in:
•	Salary sheet
•	Sales report




Accounting
Similar to Currency but:
•	Symbols aligned properly
•	Looks professional
Mostly used in:
•	Company financial reports
Date
Converts numbers into date format.
Example:
44500 → 12-02-2026
Formats available:
•	DD-MM-YYYY
•	MM/DD/YYYY
•	Long date
Time
Displays time values.
Example:
10:30 AM
22:15
Used in:
•	Attendance
•	Shift timings
Percentage (%)
Multiplies value by 100 and adds %.
Example:
0.5 → 50%
0.25 → 25%
Very important for:
•	Profit %
•	Growth %
•	Marks %
Fraction
Displays number as fraction.
Example:
0.5 → 1/2
0.25 → 1/4
Text
Treats value as text.
Example:
00123 will remain 00123
Used for:
•	Roll numbers
•	Phone numbers
•	ID numbers
Custom Format
User-defined format.
Examples:
•	Dates
•	You  can custom your own dates
